# Prettier ignore. Lives at the repo root (not .config/) so patterns anchor to
# the repo root — like .gitignore. A .config/-located ignore file anchors
# slash-bearing patterns to .config/ itself, which silently fails to match
# repo-root paths. The prettier *config* still lives in .config/prettier.config.mjs;
# this is data (an ignore list), whose conventional home is the root.
#
# node_modules is ignored by Prettier automatically; everything else is listed.
# Mirrors the ESLint global ignores in .config/eslint.config.mjs.

# Build + tooling output
**/dist/**
**/.turbo/**
**/coverage/**

# Vendored third-party bundles (e.g. the minified Cytoscape bundle the
# dashboard ships). Pretty-printing them inflates their byte size and breaks
# the bundle-weight budget tests — they must stay exactly as vendored.
**/vendor/**

# Claude Code worktrees — parallel-session checkouts live here. Never format
# another session's working tree (the `**/*` format glob would otherwise
# recurse into them).
.claude/**

# Test fixtures (intentionally unformatted — they encode exact input bytes)
fixtures/**
**/__fixtures__/**
**/*.snap

# Docs: prose is author-owned and docs/web-generated/ is machine-generated
# (web:skip/web:only voice markers must not be disturbed). Markdown is out of
# the chosen format scope; excluding all of docs/ keeps the boundary clean.
docs/**

# Lockfile is pnpm-owned
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Generated client bundle (esbuild output inlined into the dashboard report)
**/client-bundle.generated.ts

# Generated report artifacts written to the repo root by CI / the lint lane
# (bench:slo → slo-report.json, compat:matrix:check → compatibility-matrix-report.json,
# detection-quality → detection-quality-report.json). They are gitignored, but CI
# generates slo-report.json BEFORE `pnpm lint`, so without this exclusion
# `format:check` (which globs **/*.json) trips on the unformatted output and
# reddens build-and-test. These are tool output, not authored source.
slo-report.json
compatibility-matrix-report.json
detection-quality-report.json

# Packed distribution measurement inputs and schema-owned report artifacts.
# The measurement writer, not Prettier, owns their serialized bytes and hash.
.opensip-distribution/**
distribution-footprint-report*.json

# Immutable, gitignored agent-evaluation output. The report schema owns this
# serialization; running the harness before lint must not make format:check red.
packages/agent-eval/results/**

# CLI-bundled adapter catalog (generated projection of adapter manifests)
**/first-party-adapters.generated.ts

# Per-package test typecheck configs (generated by scripts/build-test-tsconfigs.mjs,
# validated by `pnpm typecheck:tests:check` — the generator, not prettier, owns them)
**/tsconfig.test.json
